# Infrastructure as Code — {{projectName}} on Azure Container Apps

Deploys {{projectName}} to **Azure Container Apps** with **Terraform**.
Everything is environment-scoped and driven by `dude iac …`, which works
identically on your laptop and in CI/CD.

**If you just want it deployed, follow [Part 1](#part-1-first-deploy-start-to-finish)
top to bottom.** The rest of this file is reference.

There is no Kubernetes here: no cluster, no kubectl, no Helm chart. Terraform
describes the container apps directly, and the platform runs them.

```
iac/
├── terraform/
│   ├── versions.tf            # providers + azurerm backend (partial)
│   ├── providers.tf           # azurerm
│   ├── variables.tf           # all inputs (sane defaults)
│   ├── main.tf                # resource group + VNet + Container Apps env + apps{{#if withPostgres}} + PostgreSQL{{/if}}
│   ├── outputs.tf             # app URL, registry URLs{{#if withPostgres}}, database{{/if}}
│   ├── bootstrap/             # one-time shared infra: state storage account + container registry
│   └── environments/
│       └── dev/
│           ├── backend.hcl        # remote-state location for this env
│           └── terraform.tfvars   # this env's sizing/knobs + the deployed image tag
└── runner/
    └── Dockerfile             # the toolchain `dude iac` runs in — yours to edit
```

